[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue with one fix queued. Counted by cause, its
reports do not share one issue. Engineering closed the ticket on 5 October, with a different
outcome for each cause.

<Callout kind="warn">
Closed does not mean fixed. Only the parser got a fix. The hint problem is won't fix, because the booking-v3 form is retired.
</Callout>

## What was merged

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The last column is the desk's own view: its ticket system had one ticket. Each cause now has a
ticket of its own, linked below.

## How each one ended

| cause    | outcome   | engineering update                       | ticket                                                                |
| -------- | --------- | ---------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `parser` | fixed     | `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales` | [closed as completed](https://github.com/pdudzinsky/support-kb-4471/issues/1)  |
| `hint`   | won't fix | booking-v3 form retired                  | [closed as not planned](https://github.com/pdudzinsky/support-kb-4471/issues/2) |

## `parser`: the shared parser read dates month first

The shared parser read every date month first. Tenants in day-first locales write the day first,
so the day and month came out swapped. Engineering fixed this.

The reports read as a one-day move stay here because the desk files by tenant. A swapped day and
month does not explain a one-day move, so this fix may not end them. If reports like these keep
coming, they need a ticket of their own.

## `hint`: the booking-v3 form asked for the month first

The booking-v3 form printed `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People typed what it told them,
month first, and the form read the date the tenant's way, day first. The parser fix did not
change what this form printed. Engineering will not fix the form, because it is retired.

Only reports through the form on a booking-v3 tenant belong here. The same tenants' app and email
reports are `parser`.

## Why one ticket hid this

- **Subjects do not tell the causes apart.** [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)
  merges on subject alone, and both causes use the same subjects.
- **Intake tags are a guess.** Intake tags a report from the browser it came in on. The cause comes
  from the tenant and the channel. The `tagged as` column shows how often the two disagree, so do
  not count by tag.
- **The export repeats reports.** The ticket system exports pages that overlap. Count unique ids,
  not rows.

## What is left

- Check that the tenants the directory lists on booking-v3 have moved off it. The export predates
  the update, so it may still list them.
- Update the [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471). It still says one issue, one fix queued.
- Replace decision 0001 with a new record. It is accepted, so it stays as written until then.

